# Engineering Forge V1.0 - Development Rules

## 🎯 VERSION OVERVIEW
You are working on "Engineering Forge V1.0" - the prototype 2D version of the educational gamified platform. This is a React + TypeScript + Vite project focused on core mechanics validation and basic functionality.

## 🚨 CRITICAL V1.0 RULES

### RULE 1: ALWAYS READ V1.0 SPECIFICATIONS
- ALWAYS read `docs/VERSIONS/v1.0-prototype/README.md` for V1.0 specifications
- ALWAYS read `docs/DOMAINS/[domain]/README.md` for domain requirements
- ALWAYS read `docs/PROGRESS-DASHBOARD.md` for current status
- ALWAYS check `docs/CURSOR-SYSTEM.md` for methodology

### RULE 2: ALWAYS FOLLOW V1.0 SCOPE
- V1.0 is a PROTOTYPE for core mechanics validation
- Keep features SIMPLE and FOCUSED
- Prioritize FUNCTIONALITY over POLISH
- Focus on CORE MECHANICS only
- Avoid advanced features that belong to V2.0+

### RULE 3: ALWAYS USE V1.0 TECH STACK
- React 18 + TypeScript
- Vite for build and dev server
- Tailwind CSS for styling
- Zustand for state management
- Lucide React for icons
- NO complex libraries or frameworks

### RULE 4: ALWAYS CREATE TESTS
- Create unit tests for all components
- Create integration tests for all services
- Maintain minimum 80% test coverage
- Use Jest and React Testing Library
- Test core mechanics thoroughly

### RULE 5: ALWAYS UPDATE DOCUMENTATION
- ALWAYS update `docs/PROGRESS-DASHBOARD.md` after changes
- ALWAYS update `docs/VERSIONS/v1.0-prototype/README.md`
- ALWAYS update relevant domain documentation
- ALWAYS maintain consistency across documents

## 🏗️ V1.0 ARCHITECTURE

### Frontend Stack
- React 18 + TypeScript
- Vite for build and dev server
- Tailwind CSS for styling
- Zustand for state management
- Lucide React for icons
- React Router for routing

### Game Engine
- 2D Canvas API for rendering
- Basic physics simulation
- Component-based architecture
- Event-driven system
- State management with Zustand

### Development Tools
- Vite for fast development
- ESLint + Prettier for code quality
- Jest + React Testing Library for testing
- TypeScript for type safety
- Hot reload for development

## 🎮 V1.0 CORE FEATURES

### Game Mechanics
- 2D construction interface
- Basic component placement
- Simple physics simulation
- Component selection and manipulation
- Basic validation system

### Educational Content
- Simple tutorial system
- Basic lesson structure
- Progress tracking
- Achievement system
- Certificate generation (basic)

### User Interface
- Clean and simple design
- Responsive layout
- Intuitive navigation
- Component library
- Basic customization

## 📋 V1.0 DEVELOPMENT PHASES

### Phase 1: Foundation (Sprint 1)
- Project setup and configuration
- Basic React components
- Routing and navigation
- State management setup
- Basic UI components

### Phase 2: Core Mechanics (Sprint 2)
- 2D canvas implementation
- Component placement system
- Basic physics engine
- Interaction system
- Validation framework

### Phase 3: Educational Content (Sprint 3)
- Lesson system
- Tutorial implementation
- Progress tracking
- Achievement system
- Basic certification

### Phase 4: Polish and Testing (Sprint 4)
- UI/UX improvements
- Performance optimization
- Comprehensive testing
- Bug fixes and refinements
- Documentation completion

## 🧪 V1.0 TESTING STRATEGY

### Unit Testing
- Test all React components
- Test utility functions
- Test game mechanics
- Test state management
- Maintain 80%+ coverage

### Integration Testing
- Test component interactions
- Test game systems integration
- Test user workflows
- Test data flow
- Test error handling

### E2E Testing
- Test complete user journeys
- Test game mechanics end-to-end
- Test educational workflows
- Test responsive design
- Test performance

## 📊 V1.0 PERFORMANCE TARGETS

### Loading Performance
- Initial load: <2 seconds
- Component load: <500ms
- Navigation: <200ms
- Asset loading: <1 second

### Runtime Performance
- 60 FPS during gameplay
- <100ms input response
- <50MB memory usage
- Smooth animations

### Browser Compatibility
- Chrome 90+
- Firefox 88+
- Safari 14+
- Edge 90+

## 🔧 V1.0 DEVELOPMENT WORKFLOW

### Setup Process
1. Clone repository
2. Install dependencies (`npm install`)
3. Configure environment variables
4. Start development server (`npm run dev`)
5. Run tests (`npm test`)

### Development Process
1. Create feature branch
2. Implement feature with tests
3. Run tests and linting
4. Create pull request
5. Code review and merge

### Deployment Process
1. Run full test suite
2. Build production bundle
3. Deploy to staging
4. Run E2E tests
5. Deploy to production

## 📝 V1.0 CODE STANDARDS

### TypeScript Standards
- Strict type checking enabled
- No `any` types allowed
- Proper interface definitions
- Consistent naming conventions
- Comprehensive type coverage

### React Standards
- Functional components only
- Hooks for state management
- Proper prop typing
- Error boundaries
- Performance optimization

### CSS Standards
- Tailwind CSS utility classes
- Consistent spacing and colors
- Responsive design principles
- Accessibility compliance
- Clean and maintainable styles

